 ## Root Cause
  
  -b (build all) was run, but drm-lease-manager (build ID 1) was never compiled because either:
  
  • meson / ninja-build weren't installed at the time, or
  • The build step failed silently and the -g git clone was taken as "done"
  
  The binary was never placed in $PATH (/usr/local/bin), and the runtime dir /var/local/run/drm-lease-manager/ was never created.
  ──────
  ## Fix — Run in this order
  
  1. Install missing build tools + packages:
  
    cd /home/senay/Projects/multiseat
    sudo ./multiseat-mint.sh -gp
  
  2. Rebuild drm-lease-manager (ID 1):
  
    sudo ./multiseat-mint.sh -b 1
  
  3. Refresh library symlinks (creates /usr/lib/libdlmclient* and the systemd service):
  
    sudo ./multiseat-mint.sh -l
  
  4. Create the runtime directory (the script expects it to exist before drm-lease-manager runs):
  
    sudo mkdir -p /var/local/run/drm-lease-manager
  
  5. Start multiseat:
  
    sudo ./multiseat-mint.sh -s
  ──────
  │ Tip
  │ After step 2 succeeds, you should see /usr/local/bin/drm-lease-manager exist. Verify with:
  │
  │   which drm-lease-manager
  │
  │ If it prints nothing, the meson install step failed — check the build output for errors.

